    "title": "Who from Longview Metro area's former high school athletes will participate in games on Saturday, Dec. 6? - Longview Times",
    "text": "Saturday, Dec. 6 will feature competition from these former Longview Metro area high school standouts.\nGage Parker\nArkansas Tech Wonder Boys\nJunior\n6′1″ 285\nElysian Fields High School\nHometown: De Berry\nNext Game: vs. West Texas A&M Buffaloes, Saturday, Dec. 6, 12 p.m.\nJackson Richardson\nHarding Bison\nSophomore\n6′4″ 205\nTatum High School\nHometown: Tatum\nNext Game: vs. Texas–Permian Basin Falcons, Saturday, Dec. 6, 1 p.m.\nJalen Hale\nAlabama Crimson Tide\nSophomore\n6′1″ 197\nLongview High School\nHometown: Longview\nNext Game: vs. Georgia Bulldogs, Saturday, Dec. 6, 3 p.m.\nKason Brooks\nHarding Bison\nFreshman\n5′11″ 210\nLongview High School\nHometown: Longview\nNext Game: vs. Texas–Permian Basin Falcons, Saturday, Dec. 6, 1 p.m.\nLuke Sigler\nTexas–Permian Basin Falcons\nFreshman\n6′1″ 210\nTatum High School\nHometown: Tatum\nNext Game: vs. Harding Bison, Saturday, Dec. 6, 1 p.m.\nTa’Erik Tate\nStephen F. Austin Lumberjacks\nWide receiver\nSophomore\n5′11″ 187\nGilmer High School\nHometown: Gilmer\nNext Game: vs. Abilene Christian Wildcats, Saturday, Dec. 6, 1 p.m.",
